<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's environment (decision D102; named the room until D248),
  run as the root session. Its invoked children are its participants: join
  is an invoke starting, leave is the invoke ending (cancelled, done, or
  failed). It keeps membership, delivers what enters it, and supervises
  its bots.

    present (parallel) { keeping, supervising.floppy { running.floppy
      (invokes floppy) -> recovering.floppy -> backoff.floppy ->
      running.floppy | exhausted.floppy (final); left.floppy (final) } }

  Participants: present invokes the floppy bot (bots/floppy/floppy.scx) as
  its child "floppy", with the environment's id (the root's _sessionid,
  decision D106) as <param name="environment"> and the devices it holds as
  <param name="owned_devices">, and what each of its devices sits on as
  <param name="placed_on"> (decision D159); the bot activates on joining
  (decision D107). An environment with devices (devices/<name>/<name>.scx, decision
  D105) invokes them in the same state, before its bots, and names in
  holdings which bot holds which; this environment has none. A child's
  _sessionid is <the environment's _sessionid>.<invoke id> (scxml.rs,
  decision D110), so each bot's owned_devices maps each device's reference,
  its invoke id, to its address before anything starts. A device is a
  participant too: it receives the broadcasts, and its bot.input goes to
  the bots holding it. participants holds the invoke ids of the children
  present invokes, set on its entry; a child's done.invoke.<id> (the bot's
  session ended in inactive or degraded) or error.communication.<id> (it
  failed) removes it, and the environment logs the event's invokeid and
  data (the bot's donedata). A failed send (error.communication with no
  invokeid) removes nobody.

  Supervision (decision D158): each bot
  runs in its own region of present, supervising.<bot>, which invokes it in
  running.<bot>. A bot that leaves degraded (its donedata has a reason),
  after a failed activation (it sent bot.activating.failed), or failed
  (error.communication.<bot>) is restarted: recovering.<bot> counts the
  failed attempt and waits in backoff.<bot> (a doubling backoff from
  backoff_initial_ms, capped at backoff_max_ms) before
  running.<bot> invokes it again, logged bot.restarted {participant,
  attempt, delay_ms}; when another attempt would not fit max_restarts the
  bot is left, logged bot.exhausted {participant, attempts}
  (exhausted.<bot>). A bot that has run stable_after_ms has its attempts
  reset, counted once from its first bot.activated (starting.<bot>,
  serving.<bot>; a reboot does not re-arm it). A bot that leaves on
  bot.deactivate, or is sent one while it waits in backoff.<bot>, is not
  restarted (left.<bot>). The leave and the activation are announced to
  the regions as bot.left {participant, restart} and bot.running
  {participant} [placeholder names, D248], internal
  events of the environment (participant
  null for a failed send, which names no invoke and no region takes).

  Sound (decision D103): an environment.sound or environment.visual from a
  participant (a bot's communication sends its speaking's playout to
  #_scxml_ + the environment's id; a device sends to its parent) or from
  the host is logged, which keeps the environment's broadcasts in the
  run's records, and goes to every participant that perceives it, the
  emitter included (its efference copy withholds its own speech). A visual
  stimulus reaches every participant. A sound's level where a participant
  is follows the free-field law, from the emitter's amplitude_db
  (dB SPL at 1 m) and the distance d between the sender's placement (the
  origin: placements[_event.invokeid], so only a placed child has one) and
  the participant's: received_level_db = amplitude_db - 20 log10(max(d,
  0.01) / 1) (a 1 cm clamp); the participant receives it, with that
  received_level_db, only when it is at least its threshold_db. With no
  amplitude, no origin, or no placement there is nothing to measure: the
  participant hears it, and received_level_db is left as it was. A sound
  too quiet for everyone is sent to nobody.

  Host input (decision D108) enters the environment and is routed by what
  its payload says, never by who sent it: bot.ability.communication.input
  goes to each participant its target_ids names, and to every participant
  when target_ids is empty (the input is ambient);
  environment.sound and environment.visual go to every participant (a
  broadcast); bot.deactivate and bot.input go to every bot.

  Records: each event a bot sends its parent (bot.activated,
  bot.processing.completed, ...) is logged as <log label="EVENT"> with its
  data as JSON, which keeps the run's records. A voice embedding is
  biometric and is never written: an identity in source_ids or target_ids
  that is an array of numbers is written as <biometric:VoiceEmbedding>.

  Contracts: every event the environment takes references its one schema file
  (../../bots/floppy/schemas/ for the body's events,
  ../../abilities/schemas/ for the abilities'); scx run refuses host input
  they reject (machine-invalid-input).

  Running: scx run with an env file and this document (bots/floppy/README.md
  gives the grants and variables the bot needs).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="environment" initial="present">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The invoke ids of the participants present, and the one being sent
         to. -->
    <data id="participants" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="participant" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Which devices each bot holds: bot invoke id to device invoke ids
         (decision D105). Its keys are the bots; every other participant
         is a device. -->
    <data id="holdings" expr="({floppy: []})"/>
    <!-- Where each participant is, the quietest sound it hears, and what
         it sits on: invoke id to {position: {x, y, z} in metres,
         threshold_db in dB SPL, on?: an object's id}. A participant with
         none hears every sound. -->
    <data id="placements" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The physical things participants sit on (a desk, a table, a
         shelf): their ids. An
         object does nothing; it shows only through what sits on it. -->
    <data id="objects" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- Supervision (decision D158): the
         consecutive failed attempts each bot may make, its backoff, and
         how long it runs before its attempts are reset; each bot's failed
         attempts and whether its last activation failed. -->
    <data id="supervision" expr="({max_restarts: 5, backoff_initial_ms: 1000, backoff_max_ms: 60000, stable_after_ms: 60000})"/>
    <data id="attempts" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="activation_failed" expr="({})"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="environment.js"/>

  <parallel id="present">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="participants" expr="['floppy']"/>
    </onentry>
    <!-- Membership and delivery: present's own transitions, below. -->
    <state id="keeping"/>
    <!-- The bot floppy, supervised. -->
    <state id="supervising.floppy" initial="running.floppy">
      <state id="running.floppy" initial="starting.floppy">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="participants" expr="joined('floppy')"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="stable.floppy"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="floppy" type="scxml" src="../../bots/floppy/floppy.scx">
          <param name="environment" expr="_sessionid"/>
          <param name="owned_devices" expr="ownedDevices('floppy')"/>
          <param name="placed_on" expr="placedOn('floppy')"/>
        </invoke>
        <!-- Stable after stable_after_ms from its first bot.activated (armed
             once, in serving, which it enters on activation); a reboot's
             activation does not re-arm it. -->
        <state id="starting.floppy">
          <transition event="bot.running" cond="isFor(_event, 'floppy')" target="serving.floppy"/>
        </state>
        <state id="serving.floppy">
          <onentry>
            <send id="stable.floppy" event="bot.stable" delayexpr="stableDelay()">
              <param name="participant" expr="'floppy'"/>
            </send>
          </onentry>
        </state>
        <transition event="bot.stable" cond="isFor(_event, 'floppy')">
          <assign location="attempts.floppy" expr="0"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.left" cond="isRestartable(_event, 'floppy')" target="recovering.floppy"/>
        <transition event="bot.left" cond="isFor(_event, 'floppy')" target="left.floppy"/>
      </state>
      <state id="recovering.floppy">
        <transition cond="isWithinBudget('floppy')" target="backoff.floppy">
          <assign location="attempts.floppy" expr="nextAttempt('floppy')"/>
        </transition>
        <transition target="exhausted.floppy">
          <log label="bot.exhausted" expr="exhaustedJson('floppy')"/>
        </transition>
      </state>
      <state id="backoff.floppy">
        <onentry>
          <send id="restart.floppy" event="bot.restart" delayexpr="backoffDelay('floppy')">
            <param name="participant" expr="'floppy'"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="restart.floppy"/>
        </onexit>
        <!-- A stop while it waits: it is not restarted. -->
        <transition event="bot.deactivate" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.deactivate.json" target="left.floppy"/>
        <transition event="bot.restart" cond="isFor(_event, 'floppy')" target="running.floppy">
          <log label="bot.restarted" expr="restartedJson('floppy')"/>
          <assign location="activation_failed.floppy" expr="false"/>
        </transition>
      </state>
      <final id="exhausted.floppy"/>
      <final id="left.floppy"/>
    </state>

    <!-- Leave: a participant that finished or failed, announced to its
         supervisor. -->
    <transition event="done.invoke">
      <log label="done.invoke" expr="leaveJson(_event)"/>
      <assign location="participants" expr="without(_event.invokeid)"/>
      <send event="bot.left" target="#_internal">
        <content expr="leftData(_event, false)"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.communication">
      <log label="error.communication" expr="leaveJson(_event)"/>
      <assign location="participants" expr="without(_event.invokeid)"/>
      <send event="bot.left" target="#_internal">
        <content expr="leftData(_event, true)"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <!-- Host input. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json">
      <foreach array="addressees(_event.data.target_ids)" item="participant">
        <send event="bot.ability.communication.input" targetexpr="participantTarget(participant)">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </foreach>
    </transition>
    <transition event="environment.sound" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/environment.sound.json">
      <log label="environment.sound" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
      <foreach array="participants" item="participant">
        <if cond="hears(participant, _event)">
          <send event="environment.sound" targetexpr="participantTarget(participant)">
            <content expr="delivered(participant, _event)"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </foreach>
    </transition>
    <transition event="environment.visual" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/environment.visual.json">
      <log label="environment.visual" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
      <foreach array="participants" item="participant">
        <send event="environment.visual" targetexpr="participantTarget(participant)">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </foreach>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.deactivate" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.deactivate.json">
      <foreach array="bots()" item="participant">
        <send event="bot.deactivate" targetexpr="participantTarget(participant)">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </foreach>
    </transition>
    <!-- bot.input: from a device, to the bots that hold it, with
         target_device stamped as the device's reference; from the host,
         to every bot. The recipients and the stamp are chosen from
         _event.invokeid in exprs (decision D108). -->
    <transition event="bot.input" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.input.json">
      <foreach array="inputRecipients(_event)" item="participant">
        <send event="bot.input" targetexpr="participantTarget(participant)">
          <content expr="inputData(_event)"/>
        </send>
      </foreach>
    </transition>

    <!-- What the bots emit. -->
    <transition event="bot.activated" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.activated.json">
      <log label="bot.activated" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
      <send event="bot.running" target="#_internal">
        <content expr="activatedData(_event)"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.activating.failed" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.activating.failed.json">
      <log label="bot.activating.failed" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
      <assign location="activation_failed" expr="activationFailedOf(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.deactivated" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.deactivated.json">
      <log label="bot.deactivated" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.processing.completed" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.processing.completed.json">
      <log label="bot.processing.completed" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.processing.failed" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.processing.failed.json">
      <log label="bot.processing.failed" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.processing.timed_out" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.processing.timed_out.json">
      <log label="bot.processing.timed_out" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.processing.cancel.timed_out" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.processing.cancel.timed_out.json">
      <log label="bot.processing.cancel.timed_out" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.degraded" event:schema="../../bots/floppy/schemas/bot.degraded.json">
      <log label="bot.degraded" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.reboot" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.reboot.json">
      <log label="bot.reboot" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.output" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.speaking.output.json">
      <log label="bot.ability.speaking.output" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.communication.failed" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.communication.failed.json">
      <log label="bot.ability.communication.failed" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.conversation.failed.json">
      <log label="bot.ability.conversation.failed" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.output" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.conversation.output.json">
      <log label="bot.ability.conversation.output" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.listening.failed" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.listening.failed.json">
      <log label="bot.ability.listening.failed" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.failed.json">
      <log label="bot.ability.failed" expr="eventDataJson(_event)"/>
    </transition>
  </parallel>
</scxml>
